      { t: 'code', q: 'Write a decorator `count_calls` that adds a `.calls` attribute to the wrapped function, counting how many times it ran.', starter: 'import functools\n\ndef count_calls(fn):\n    pass\n\n@count_calls\ndef ping():\n    return "pong"\n', tests: 'assert ping() == "pong", "must return the original result"\nping(); ping()\nassert ping.calls == 3, "expected 3, got " + str(getattr(ping, "calls", None))\nprint("Counted.")', sol: 'import functools\n\ndef count_calls(fn):\n    @functools.wraps(fn)\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        wrapper.calls += 1\n        return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n    wrapper.calls = 0\n    return wrapper\n\n@count_calls\ndef ping():\n    return "pong"', hint: 'Define wrapper, set wrapper.calls = 0 before returning it, and increment inside.', e: 'Storing state on the wrapper object avoids nonlocal bookkeeping and is easy to inspect.' }
