      { t: 'code', q: 'Rewrite this O(n²) function to run in O(n): `has_duplicates(items)` returns True if any value appears twice.', starter: 'def has_duplicates(items):\n    # slow version: for i in range(len(items)): for j in ...\n    pass\n', tests: 'assert has_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 1]) is True\nassert has_duplicates([1, 2, 3]) is False\nassert has_duplicates([]) is False\nbig = list(range(60000)) + [7]\nimport time\nstart = time.perf_counter()\nassert has_duplicates(big) is True\nassert time.perf_counter() - start < 1.0, "too slow: use a set, not nested loops"\nprint("Fast.")', sol: 'def has_duplicates(items):\n    seen = set()\n    for x in items:\n        if x in seen:\n            return True\n        seen.add(x)\n    return False', hint: 'Track what you have seen in a set, or compare len(set(items)) with len(items).', e: 'Trading memory for time with a hash set is the single most common algorithmic speedup.' }
